'''Josèp Bernat''' (11 June 1834 – 4 July 1903) was the third [[President of the Baliscan Confederation|President of Balisca]], presiding from 1868 until 1876. Josèp's administration continued many of the policies of his predecessor with little deviation, which led to [[Renaiximiento|widespread dissatisfaction]] and social unrest throughout his tenure. He ultimately resigned from the presidency following the failure of the [[Siege of Castejón (1874)|Siege of Castejón]] during the [[Cantonal War]]. 

